Here's the raw recipe — save it wherever you keep prompts (a file, a note, paste it into a new session):

---

**Chrome Browser Automation via AppleScript + JavaScript**

Prerequisites:
- Chrome → View → Developer → "Allow JavaScript from Apple Events" (must be enabled once)
- macOS Terminal with osascript access

Core patterns:

```bash
# Navigate to a URL
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome" to set URL of active tab of front window to "https://example.com"'

# Execute JS and get result
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome" to execute front window'\''s active tab javascript "document.title"'

# List all tabs
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome"
  set res to ""
  set tc to count of tabs of front window
  repeat with i from 1 to tc
    set res to res & i & ": " & URL of tab i of front window & linefeed
  end repeat
  return res
end tell'

# Switch to specific tab
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome" to set active tab index of front window to 4'

# Store long JS results in document.title (workaround for osascript output limits)
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome" to execute front window'\''s active tab javascript "
fetch(\"/api/something\", {credentials: \"include\"}).then(function(r) { return r.text(); }).then(function(t) { document.title = t.substring(0, 800); });
\"fetching...\";
"'
sleep 3
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome" to execute front window'\''s active tab javascript "document.title"'

# Click buttons that need full mouse event sequence (React/Radix UI apps)
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome" to execute front window'\''s active tab javascript "
var btn = document.querySelector(\"button[aria-haspopup=menu]\");
btn.scrollIntoView({block: \"center\"});
var events = [\"pointerdown\", \"mousedown\", \"pointerup\", \"mouseup\", \"click\"];
for (var e = 0; e < events.length; e++) {
  btn.dispatchEvent(new MouseEvent(events[e], {bubbles: true, cancelable: true, view: window}));
}
\"clicked\";
"'

# Async automation loop (for React apps with dialogs/confirmations)
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome" to execute front window'\''s active tab javascript "
async function doStuff() {
  // ... click, await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 800)), check DOM, repeat
  return \"done\";
}
doStuff().then(function(r) { document.title = r; });
\"running...\";
"'

# Discover API endpoints from any SPA (intercept network calls)
osascript -e 'tell application "Google Chrome" to execute front window'\''s active tab javascript "
var entries = performance.getEntriesByType(\"resource\");
var apis = [];
for (var i = 0; i < entries.length; i++) {
  if (entries[i].name.indexOf(\"api\") > -1) apis.push(entries[i].name);
}
apis.join(\"\\n\");
"'
```

Key gotchas:
- `osascript` JS returns `missing value` if the expression returns undefined — always end with a string expression
- Use `var` not `const`/`let` for reliability in some contexts
- React/Radix UI buttons need full pointer event sequence, not just `.click()`
- For async operations, store result in `document.title` and poll with `sleep + read title`
- Single quotes inside osascript: escape as `'\''`
- Authenticated fetch calls work because you're in the user's browser session (cookies included)

---

Paste this into any future session when you need browser automation. Works on any website, not just claude.ai.

